'BEL Probationary Engineer Recruitment 2026: 350 Posts, Applications Open 28 October, Deadline 18 November 2026',
'',
'Bharat Electronics Limited has opened applications for 350 BEL Probationary Engineer posts in Electronics and Mechanical disciplines, with the online window running from 28 October 2026 to 18 November 2026.',
'',
$$<p>Bharat Electronics Limited (BEL) has opened applications for 350 BEL Probationary Engineer posts, with the online window running from 28 October 2026 to 18 November 2026. The BEL Probationary Engineer notification, Advertisement No. 17556/HR/All-India/2026, was published on 28 October 2026, and the application portal opened at 2:00 PM on the same day, The Times of India reported. The posts are in E-II Grade and cover the Electronics and Mechanical disciplines for production and support services roles across BEL units and offices.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance: BEL Probationary Engineer recruitment 2026</th><th>Detail</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Bharat Electronics Limited (BEL), a Government of India enterprise under the Ministry of Defence</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Probationary Engineer, E-II Grade</td></tr><tr><td>Advertisement number</td><td>17556/HR/All-India/2026</td></tr><tr><td>Notification date</td><td>28 October 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Total vacancies</td><td>350, including backlog vacancies</td></tr><tr><td>Electronics vacancies</td><td>200</td></tr><tr><td>Mechanical vacancies</td><td>150</td></tr><tr><td>Applications open</td><td>28 October 2026 at 2:00 PM</td></tr><tr><td>Application deadline</td><td>18 November 2026 at 11:59 PM</td></tr><tr><td>Pay scale</td><td>Rs. 40,000 to Rs. 1,40,000, with an approximate annual cost to company of Rs. 13 lakh</td></tr><tr><td>Application fee</td><td>Rs. 1,180 for General, EWS and OBC (NCL) candidates; SC, ST, PwBD and Ex-servicemen candidates are exempt</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Computer-based test of 85 marks followed by an interview of 15 marks</td></tr><tr><td>Computer-based test</td><td>Tentatively scheduled for 22 December 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Official website</td><td>bel-india.in</td></tr></table>
<h2>BEL Probationary Engineer vacancies: 200 Electronics and 150 Mechanical posts</h2>
<p>The application is discipline-specific. BEL has advertised 200 Probationary Engineer posts in Electronics and 150 in Mechanical, 350 in total including backlog vacancies, for BEL production and support services departments.</p>
<p>BEL has listed potential job locations across its units and offices in Bengaluru, Ghaziabad, Pune, Nagpur, Navi Mumbai, Hyderabad, Chennai and other locations in India, The Times of India reported. Candidates should therefore not assume a posting in one named city, and the three-week window leaves little room for a late start.</p>
<h2>BEL Probationary Engineer eligibility: degree, class and age limit</h2>
<p>Candidates must hold a B.E., B.Tech. or four-year B.Sc. Engineering degree in the prescribed Electronics or Mechanical disciplines, Jagran Josh reported. A first-class qualification is required, while pass-class candidates are eligible under the stated provisions for SC, ST and PwBD categories.</p>
<p>For Electronics, the eligible specialisations include Electronics, Electronics and Communication, Electronics and Telecommunication, and Communication and Telecommunication, Jagran Josh reported. For Mechanical posts, candidates must hold a degree in Mechanical Engineering. Candidates with first-class AMIE, AMIETE or GIETE qualifications in the specified disciplines are also eligible, Jagran Josh reported.</p>
<p>The upper age limit for Unreserved and EWS candidates is 25 years as of 1 October 2026, The Times of India reported. Jagran Josh reported age relaxation of three years for OBC (NCL) candidates and five years for SC and ST candidates. Applicants close to the limit should check the notification for the exact rules for their category.</p>
<p>One caution applies to every applicant: the specialisation named on the degree certificate must match the branch chosen in the application, and a mismatch can lead to rejection at a later stage.</p>
<h2>BEL Probationary Engineer selection: computer-based test and interview</h2>
<p>Selection will comprise a computer-based test carrying 85 marks and an interview carrying 15 marks, The Times of India reported. The test will contain 125 questions to be answered in 120 minutes, and one-fourth of a mark will be deducted for each incorrect answer, so blind guessing across the whole paper is a poor plan.</p>
<p>The computer-based test is tentatively scheduled for 22 December 2026, Jagran Josh reported, so candidates should watch bel-india.in for the confirmed schedule rather than treating that date as final. The interview carries 15 marks out of the 100-mark selection total, enough to change the final order, so preparation should cover both the written paper and the interview.</p>
<h2>Why the BEL Probationary Engineer notification matters for engineering graduates</h2>
<p>BEL is a Navratna public sector undertaking under the Ministry of Defence that designs and manufactures professional electronics systems for defence and related sectors. A Probationary Engineer post in E-II Grade therefore offers a route into public sector engineering work at the stated pay scale.</p>
<p>The application fee is Rs. 1,180 for General, EWS and OBC (NCL) candidates, comprising Rs. 1,000 plus GST, while SC, ST, PwBD and Ex-servicemen candidates are exempt, The Times of India reported. Non-payment of the fee by candidates who must pay it can lead to rejection, so the payment step should be completed and the receipt kept, with the degree certificate, category certificate where applicable, photograph and signature ready before starting the form.</p>
<h2>How to apply for the BEL Probationary Engineer posts</h2>
<ol>
<li>Visit bel-india.in and locate the recruitment notification under Advertisement No. 17556/HR/All-India/2026.</li>
<li>Read the full notification first, including the discipline-wise eligibility conditions, the age rules and the list of locations, before starting the form.</li>
<li>Complete the online registration with a valid email address and mobile number, then log in with the credentials received after registration.</li>
<li>Fill in personal, educational and communication details, choosing the discipline that matches the specialisation on the degree certificate.</li>
<li>Upload the photograph, signature and other required documents in the format stated in the notification.</li>
<li>Pay the application fee online where applicable, and keep the payment receipt with the submitted form.</li>
<li>Review the whole form once, submit it before 11:59 PM on 18 November 2026, and download and save a copy for future reference.</li>
</ol>
<h2>A note for readers in Nepal</h2>
<p>For readers in Nepal, the limits need to be plain. BEL is an Indian public sector undertaking and the posts are based in India, so readers outside India should check the official notification's eligibility conditions before applying, rather than assuming a foreign application will be accepted. No agent can secure a BEL post, and anyone asking for a fee to arrange one should not be trusted. Apply only through bel-india.in.</p>
<p>Growentix also covers other Indian government engineering recruitment, including <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/opsc-aee-758-posts-20261027">OPSC Assistant Executive Engineer recruitment for 758 posts</a> and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/rrb-ntpc-graduate-3548-posts-20261027">RRB NTPC graduate recruitment for 3,548 posts</a>. The BEL reporting in this article is drawn from <a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/news/bel-probationary-engineer-recruitment-2026-notification-out-for-350-posts-applications-open-october-28-apply-here/articleshow/135253014.cms">The Times of India report</a> and <a href="https://www.jagranjosh.com/articles/bel-probationary-recruitment-2026-notification-out-for-350-vacancies-check-eligibility-and-apply-online-dates-1800018305-1">the Jagran Josh report</a>, with the official website given as bel-india.in.</p>$$,
